Task: Write failing Testcontainers/Flyway migration test (Red)

Summary: Added MigrationsSuite, spinning up a real Postgres via Testcontainers and
asserting Migrations.run creates the orders table with expected columns. Confirmed Red
(compile failure — Migrations didn't exist) before implementation.

Deviation encountered and fixed: the test suite failed to even start Testcontainers —
'Could not find a valid Docker environment' — despite Docker Desktop running. Root cause:
known testcontainers-java/docker-java bug (testcontainers/testcontainers-java#11210,
#11212, #11360) — bundled docker-java hardcodes API version 1.32, rejected by this
machine's Docker Engine 29.5.2 (MinAPIVersion 1.40). Fixed via a
docker-java.properties classpath file pinning api.version=1.44. Documented in
tech-stack.md's Deferred Concerns per workflow.md step 7. Also needed a fresh sbt
process (sbt's background server retains its env from first launch, so env var changes
in a new shell invocation don't reach it) and confirming Docker Desktop's daemon was
actually running (not just the CLI client).

